{"name":"Gellibrand","hex":"#b5acb2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gellibrand","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A town in the Shire of Colac Otway, Victoria, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gellibrand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Division of Gellibrand","blocks":[{"text":"The Division of Gellibrand is an Australian Electoral Division in Victoria. The division was created in 1949 and is named after Joseph Gellibrand, a pioneer settler of the Melbourne area. It is located in the industrial inner western suburbs of Melbourne."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Division_of_Gellibrand","wikidata":"Q2973604"},{"title":"Gellibrand, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Gellibrand is a town in south west Victoria, Australia. The town is located in the Otway Ranges midway between the Princes Highway and Great Ocean Road in the Colac Otway Shire, 176 kilometres (109 mi) south west of the state capital, Melbourne. At the 2016 census, Gellibrand had a population of 210. Gellibrand is home to the Otway Districts Demons Football and Netball Club, who play Australian Rules Football and participate in the Colac & District Football League."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gellibrand%2C_Victoria","wikidata":"Q5530464"},{"title":"Gellibrand (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Gellibrand is a surname. For its etymology, see Gillibrand, of which Gellibrand is a variant. Around 2016, thirteen people in Great Britain bore the name, and none in Ireland. At the 1881 census of Great Britain, twelve people bore the name, located predominantly in London."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gellibrand_(surname)","wikidata":"Q16807890"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Joseph_Gellibrand.jpg/250px-Joseph_Gellibrand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/Joseph_Gellibrand.jpg?